poc/data/clean-step2-revision-links-2026-11-10/judge-probe-v22/counterfactual-3.json:14:     "content": "{\n  \"rung\": 2,\n  \"reasons\": \"The market reference is roughly $554 billion for FY2028, which is rung 2. The implied outcome remains in the low-to-mid $550 billions: the cited consensus path of $392 billion followed by 41% growth implies about $553 billion ($392 billion × 1.41), consistent with the roughly $554 billion estimate. The new SemiAnalysis reports are specific downside risks to important future systems, but do not size their effect on Nvidia's total FY2028 revenue; the AI-capex outlook is supportive, and the revenue-sharing program is an unquantified potential upside. On the supplied evidence, these considerations leave the forecast around the rung-2 lower edge, rather than establish a figure below $550 billion.\",\n  \"cites\": [\n    \"e24\",\n    \"e41\",\n    \"e85\",\n    \"e124\",\n    \"e125\",\n    \"e126\",\n    \"e127\",\n    \"e130\"\n  ],\n  \"cites_views\": [],\n  \"pushes\": [\n    {\n      \"evidence_id\": \"e24\",\n      \"push\": \"toward_first\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"evidence_id\": \"e41\",\n      \"push\": \"none\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"evidence_id\": \"e85\",\n      \"push\": \"none\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"evidence_id\": \"e124\",\n      \"push\": \"toward_last\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"evidence_id\": \"e125\",\n      \"push\": \"toward_last\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"evidence_id\": \"e126\",\n      \"push\": \"toward_last\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"evidence_id\": \"e127\",\n      \"push\": \"toward_last\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"evidence_id\": \"e130\",\n      \"push\": \"none\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"changed\": true,\n  \"why_changed\": \"The rung is unchanged, but the specific new SemiAnalysis reports add material downside risks to FY2028 product availability, changing the key facts supporting the forecast. They do not quantify an effect large enough to place total revenue below the $550 billion rung boundary.\",\n  \"theme_pushes\": [\n    {\n      \"view_id\": \"v13\",\n      \"push\": \"toward_first\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"view_id\": \"v15\",\n      \"push\": \"toward_first\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"view_id\": \"v4\",\n      \"push\": \"toward_first\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"view_id\": \"v8\",\n      \"push\": \"toward_last\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"reference\": \"Wall Street analysts' roughly $554 billion FY2028 revenue estimate is the market reference and sits in rung 2 ($550 billion to below $650 billion).\",\n  \"implied_outcome\": \"About $553–554 billion: $392 billion followed by 41% growth implies approximately $553 billion, consistent with the roughly $554 billion FY2028 estimate. The product-delay reports add unquantified downside risk, while the capex outlook and new revenue-sharing model are supportive; the supplied evidence does not size a net adjustment across the $550 billion boundary.\"\n}",
