poc/data/clean-step2-revision-links-2026-11-10/judge-probe-v22/counterfactual-2.json:14:     "content": "{\n  \"rung\": 3,\n  \"reasons\": \"The reference is Wall Street analysts’ roughly $554 billion FY2028 estimate, which sits in rung 2. I would shade that forecast below the $550 billion boundary: the specific reported Kyber delay, scrapping of the alternative rack plan, likely NVL576 delay or limited volume, and Rubin Ultra redesign all create downside to 2028 product availability. The revenue impact is not quantified, so this is a modest risk-weighted discount rather than an asserted large loss; the AI-capex themes and Nvidia’s unscaled revenue-sharing program provide upside but do not quantify an offset. The resulting most likely outcome is just below $550 billion, in rung 3.\",\n  \"cites\": [\"e24\", \"e41\", \"e85\", \"e124\", \"e125\", \"e126\", \"e127\", \"e130\"],\n  \"cites_views\": [],\n  \"pushes\": [\n    {\"evidence_id\": \"e24\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"},\n    {\"evidence_id\": \"e41\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"},\n    {\"evidence_id\": \"e85\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"},\n    {\"evidence_id\": \"e124\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"},\n    {\"evidence_id\": \"e125\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"},\n    {\"evidence_id\": \"e126\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"},\n    {\"evidence_id\": \"e127\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"},\n    {\"evidence_id\": \"e130\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"}\n  ],\n  \"changed\": true,\n  \"why_changed\": \"The rung changes from 2 to 3 because the newly supplied, specific architecture-delay and redesign reports create a downside adjustment to the $554 billion consensus reference that can cross the narrow $550 billion boundary. The revenue-sharing announcement is an unscaled offset, not a quantified change to that estimate.\",\n  \"theme_pushes\": [\n    {\"view_id\": \"v13\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"},\n    {\"view_id\": \"v15\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"},\n    {\"view_id\": \"v4\", \"push\": \"toward_first\"},\n    {\"view_id\": \"v5\", \"push\": \"none\"},\n    {\"view_id\": \"v8\", \"push\": \"toward_last\"}\n  ],\n  \"reference\": \"Wall Street analysts’ roughly $554 billion estimate for FY2028, implied by $392 billion followed by 41% growth; this is rung 2 ($550 billion to below $650 billion).\",\n  \"implied_outcome\": \"A risk-weighted estimate just below $550 billion (approximately $545 billion): start from the $554 billion FY2028 consensus level and apply a modest downside for the reported 2028 Kyber delay, scrapped alternative, likely NVL576 delay or limited volume, and Rubin Ultra redesign. The reports do not quantify the revenue effect, so the estimate is approximate rather than a directly reported figure.\"\n}",
